t sure which extension it is, but since Quarkus 2.10.1.Final the `app.openshift.io/runtime: quarkus` label is now missing from resources generated when using `quarkus.kubernetes.deployment-target=openshift`. For some reason it is still working when setting `quarkus.kubernetes.deployment-target=knative`.\r\n\r\nYou can see this in this diff: https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus-super-heroes/commit/fe02dae8e887df95e903bda3b5a36baf6f075336?diff=unified#diff-dc6194623579af548ca3da8872f2c72c20d41fb010026243a203b2d52da3defaL48\r\n\r\nThis commit is the diff between `2.10.0.Final` & `2.10.1.Final`. There were no other commits in between the upgrade to `2.10.0.Final` (where it was behaving correctly) and `2.10.1.Final` (where it is missing).","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/26516/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/26516/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]